{
  "workflow": "wf4",
  "unit": "WF4 Integrity Guard conflict severity ranking",
  "kind": "pure",
  "id": "wf4-integrity-severity-headlines-field-mismatch",
  "description": "A DRAFT route whose lower-severity conflict is pushed FIRST and whose DUPLICATE_ACTION_ID_FIELD_MISMATCH is pushed later must headline DUPLICATE_ACTION_ID_FIELD_MISMATCH, not the first-pushed idempotency duplicate.",
  "why_it_exists": "harness/FINDINGS.md section 1: the guard used to take conflicts[0] as 'worst'. Push order is fixed (blank action_id, blank idempotency_key, duplicate idempotency_key, then per-action_id mismatch), so on a snapshot where a duplicated action_id ALSO shares its idempotency_key, the owner saw DUPLICATE_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY — the milder truth — instead of DUPLICATE_ACTION_ID_FIELD_MISMATCH, which is the condition that could put a letter in front of the wrong party and the entire reason the node exists. commit 49dd413 ranked conflicts by a declared CONFLICT_SEVERITY order so the worst is named. This scenario pushes the idempotency duplicate first (the old headline) while the field mismatch lands later, and asserts the declared order wins.",
